feat(run): --dry-run applies to all modes (fast, cycle, hybrid)

--dry-run was parsed for every mode but only hybrid acted on it; fast and cycle
silently ignored it and executed the program (e.g. `run --mode fast hello.elf
--dry-run` printed "hello" instead of the qemu command). Now every mode prints
the exact, shell-quoted command(s) it would spawn and runs nothing.

- print_dry_run (cmd_run.cpp): one shared, labeled preview printer; run_hybrid
  and run_standalone both use it, so fast/cycle/hybrid share one format. The
  per-command label is now uniform ("# command i/N: <role> [<engine>]"; hybrid's
  old "# leg" wording folded in).
- run_standalone previews via passthrough_argv (the same argv run_passthrough
  would exec), so fast/cycle show the full qemu/vsim standalone command incl.
  -bios <elf> and any post-`--` args.
- --dry-run takes precedence over the interactive --gdb path in cycle (a dry run
  launches no debugger).
- docs: USER_GUIDE --dry-run note now covers all modes; run --help gains a
  --dry-run row.

Tested: new tests/andes_sim/test_andes_sim_dry_run.sh (RED first -- fast exec'd
the fixture; GREEN after) covering fast + cycle + a hybrid regression. The
hybrid dry-run smoke test (print_qemu_config) stays green. Behavioral change.

